{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1221631-need-more-conditions","id":1221631,"title":"Need more Conditions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-24T01:44:02-07:00","id":1221631,"title":"Need more Conditions","content":"Ok, so I like conditions and the lists in the core books are nice but I feel there's still a lot of room for more. However, even though I don't have problems with what could be a condition, I struggle how to represent them mechanically. The books give general guidance on how to make them and the official ones can serve as inspiration but I still have problems with, for instance, with creating &quot;Resolution clauses&quot; that would be both fitting and satisfying.<br /> <br /> Would anyone please share any custom conditions they created. Mostly interested in general ones, not the splat specific ones.<br /> <br /> For instance how would you represent Heartbroken as a condition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T04:25:09-07:00","id":1221648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1221631-need-more-conditions#post1221631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so I like conditions and the lists in the core books are nice but I feel there's still a lot of room for more. However, even though I don't have problems with what could be a condition, I struggle how to represent them mechanically. The books give general guidance on how to make them and the official ones can serve as inspiration but I still have problems with, for instance, with creating &quot;Resolution clauses&quot; that would be both fitting and satisfying.<br /> <br /> Would anyone please share any custom conditions they created. Mostly interested in general ones, not the splat specific ones.<br /> <br /> For instance how would you represent Heartbroken as a condition?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There are quite a lot of homebrew Conditions floating around the forum. Sadly my homebrewed ones are not in English and I'm sadly yo lazy to translate them.<br /> <br /> Heartbroken is surely a condition that many people have had and have strong reactions around, and ideas of how it would be implemented. You'd probably get as many answers as there are heartbroken people playing CofD <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> My initial take without giving it much though would be something like this.<br /> <br /> <br /> Heartbroken [persistent]<br /> <br /> &quot;And love, they have a way of slipping into blackness. Uncared for of slipping away.<br /> The deck is cut, the cards turned, the hand is played. And all we ever hope for burns to ashes and drifts away.<br /> Now don't let our love slip into this darkness. Don't leave me to the brokenhearted&quot;<br /> This conditions makes it impossible to regain willpower through normal means and you take a -2 penalty <br /> to Resolve and Composure.<br /> Possible sources: Heartbreaking actions such as; death of loved ones, break up, long term unrequited love, etc.<br /> Beat: succeeding in an action pertaining to overcome your heartbreak while also following your Virtue<br /> Resolution: Lowering or gaining Integrity, or fulfilling(as if it would've given willpower) your Virtue 10 times - Resolve+Composure<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T06:09:45-07:00","id":1221675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1221631-need-more-conditions#post1221631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For instance how would you represent Heartbroken as a condition?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have a lot of experience whipping up conditions on the fly, but let's do this. First things first, let's look at conditions that already exist. Broken Soulless kind of circle around the kind of listlessness you can feel when the person you love breaks your heart. I like the bit from Soulless about not being able to regain willpower through sleep or surrender. That sounds like something that happens when you're heartbroken. The -2 to social rolls and Resolve and -5 to intimidation from Broken also seems like something that might apply. It's hard to be scary when you can barely muster the energy to iron your shirt and comb your hair. That's a pretty big penalty, though, when added to the willpower penalty. How about Guilty? That gives you a -2 to Composure and Resolve when defending against Subterfuge, Empathy, and Intimidation. That has more of a feel of someone who goes straight into a rebound relationship and doesn't want to notice all the manipulation their new partner is doing.<br /> <br /> So, we have two kinds of paths we can take. We could go with the depressed and heartbroken condition or the straight-into-rebound condition. Let's assume the situation calls for the former. We have our effects now: no willpower recovery through sleep or surrender, and -2 to Resolve. (I think penalizing them for all social rolls on top of limiting willpower gain is a bit much.) Now on to Beats and Resolution.<br /> <br /> I think the Resolution is probably the easiest. I'll start there. The condition should resolve if you get back with the person who broke your heart (but something like Guilty could be a reasonable Condition to get instead) or if you replace that person with someone else (cue rebound drama.) It should also resolve if something shocks you out of your funk, like if you gain or lose Integrity. (It's hard to care about how your partner of 4 years left you for a tennis coach when you just saw someone gutted by a werewolf.)<br /> <br /> Beats could come from things like failed attempts to get your heart breaker back (another drama engine.) They could also come from when you fail a Resolve roll that has dramatic consequences for the character. (Like when your friends pressure you into a night out drinking even though you know you have a big presentation at work the next day.)<br /> <br /> That gives us:<br /> Heartbroken (Persistant)<br /> Effect: You cannot regain Willpower through sleep or surrender. You also suffer a -2 to Resolve.<br /> Beat: You fail at a serious attempt to win your partner back or when failing a Resolve roll has serious negative impact on the character.<br /> Resolution: You win back or replace the heartbreaker or gain or lose a point of Integrity.<br /> <br /> I think this works to create and help drive drama for the character, which is one of the things that should drive Beat gain. It also encourages the character resolve the condition, because it sucks not being able to easily regain willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T07:52:32-07:00","id":1221707,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8719\" data-vbnamecard=\"8719\">Florin</a> Nice execution, would regaining the point of Integrity mean 'getting over' your former partner? Because a resolution predicated only in terms of forging or reforging a relationship sounds pathological.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-24T08:31:27-07:00","id":1221716,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12191_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12191\" data-vbnamecard=\"12191\">Malus</a> I would see gaining a point of Integrity as moving on. You're more secure in who you are without that person in your life now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}